# CMMC L1 / NIST 800-171 3.1.1 - Limit access to authorized users
# Platform: M365 (Entra ID)
# Check type: m365_graph_query against /users

META
    esp_id `cmmc-l1-3-1-1-m365-authorized-accounts-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `m365`
    criticality `high`

    title `CMMC L1 AC.L1-3.1.1: Limit information system access to authorized users`
    description `Validates that all Entra ID user accounts are personalized (have a userPrincipalName) and have a recognized userType (Member or Guest). No shared, anonymous, or default-credential accounts may exist in the directory.`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `m365,cmmc-l1,nist-800-171,3-1-1,ac,access-control,user-identification`

    control_mapping `NIST-800-171:3.1.1`
    control_objective `3.1.1`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `M365:tenant:identity-baseline`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `7`
    recommendation `Audit /users for any account without a userPrincipalName or with an unrecognized userType. Replace any shared or anonymous accounts with named per-user identities.`

    component_id `comp-m365-identity`

    impl_3_1_1 `Information system access is limited to authorized users via the identity provider. Every directory account is personalized with a unique userPrincipalName, allowing each authentication and authorization decision to attribute to a specific principal. No shared, anonymous, or generic-credential accounts are present; every user is classified as either Member (internal) or Guest (external invited), enabling per-class policy application. Account lifecycle (provisioning, modification, deactivation) is administered through tenant administration interfaces with full audit logging.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT all_users
        path `users`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE all_users_personalized
        found boolean = true
        record
            field rows.*.userPrincipalName string contains `@`
            field rows.*.userType string != ``
        record_end
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN m365_graph_query
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF all_users_personalized
            OBJECT_REF all_users
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
